---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PostCard from '../PostCard.astro';
import { getPosts } from '../../lib/content';

const posts = await getPosts();
---
<Base title="Blog" description="Write-ups on embedded software, rockets and hardware by Shivam Desai.">
  <section class="container head">
    <p class="label">Blog</p>
    <h1 class="h-display title">Notes from the bench</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      At university I worked on a lot of designs and projects, almost always against tight deadlines. I tried to
      approach each one from first principles, but real constraints often meant the pragmatic option had to take
      over, and the goal became to make a working system. It kills me to leave them like that. This blog is my chance to
      revisit those projects: how each one was designed, where pragmatism won out, and how I would rebuild it now
      from the ground up into a deterministic, performant system.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container list" aria-label="Posts">
    {posts.length === 0 ? <p class="muted">The first post is on its way.</p> : posts.map((p) => <PostCard post={p} />)}
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .head {
    padding-top: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px);
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .title {
    margin: 12px 0 16px;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6.4vw, 92px);
  }
  /* Same style as the summary on experience pages. */
  .intro {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 680px;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.6vw, 21px);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 32px 20px;
    padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px);
  }
</style>
